        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T18:04:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`finish()` returns the subspan from `fStartingOffset` to the end of the data. Setting `fStartingOffset` inside `finish()` would change the behavior for places where `finish()` is called multiple times.\n\ni.e. starting offset gets continually incremented, causing the finish value to return only what was just added rather than the complete value. \n\nI guess in that case I should change the `finish()` call sites to also explicitly request the subspan starting from 0 instead of `fStartingOffset`?",
      "parentUuid": "aaf2a9fc_f9a7b11e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "469c58b8c69777278c44e9adc824bda3d4de2c89",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
